 bill please?</article-title><source>Bull World Health Organ</source><year>2005</year><volume>83</volume><fpage>78</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15682254</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Creese</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Parker</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><source>Cost analysis in primary health care &#x02013; A training manual for programme managers</source><year>1994</year><publisher-name>WHO, Geneva</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Over</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The effect of scale on cost projections for a primary health care programmes in a developing country</article-title><source>Soc Sci and Med</source><year>1986</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>351</fpage><lpage>360</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3083511</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0277-9536(86)90134-6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Nepal Rastra Bank</collab></person-group><source>Quart Econ Bull (Mid July 2005), Kathmandu, Nepal</source><volume>XXXIX</volume></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Ministry of Finance of Nepal</collab></person-group><source>Economic Survey Current Economic Scenario</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name>Kathmandu; Nepal Rastra Bank</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sinanovic</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Kumaranayake</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Financing and cost-effectiveness analysis of public-private partnerships: pr